# Shared annotation identity: polymorphic function with repeated type variable
# [f: [fn [x@a y@a] $x]] demonstrates that multiple params can share the same annotation identity.
# The function should be polymorphic (\forall a. Fn(a, a) -> a), allowing any type as long as both args match.
[f: [fn [let x@a y@a] x]
 result: [f 42 42]]
=== out
Dict({"f": Function(x, y), "result": Int(42)})
